1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,713
Three numbers answer most decibel questions without a calculator.

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:11,054
Doubling the intensity adds three decibels, because ten log two is three.

3
00:00:11,054 --> 00:00:15,768
Multiplying it by ten adds exactly ten decibels.

4
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:22,877
And doubling your distance from a point source quarters the intensity, so the level falls by six decibels.

